  "strategy": "1. Approach and rationale\n- We are developing a multi-resolution optimization strategy that leverages hierarchical representations to escape local optima. The core idea is to represent the signal with varying levels of resolution and project constraints hierarchically, allowing us to balance exploration and exploitation effectively.\n- The central optimization problem is non-convex with a large search space, making it challenging to find the global minimum using standard methods. Our approach addresses this by:\n  - Using iterative hierarchical representations with increasing resolution\n  - Maintaining strict constraint satisfaction through layered projections\n  - Combining global exploration with local refinement phases\n  - Incorporating gradient information for faster convergence\n- Key advantages include the ability to navigate complex landscapes by leveraging multiple scales and aggressive repair mechanisms to ensure constraint satisfaction.\n\n2. Mathematical specification\n- Variables: \n  - Base resolution h0 \u2208 [0,1]^560, integer sum = 280\n  - Hierarchical representation: h_i^{(m)} \u2208 [0,1]^N, varying resolution N (powers of two)\n- Objective: Minimize C5 = max_k (np.correlate(h, 1-h, mode='full')*(2.0/n0)\n- Constraints:\n  - Integral constraint: \u222bh dx = 1\n  - Boundedness: 0 \u2264 h(x) \u2264 1 \u2200x\n  - Hierarchical consistency: h0 can be reconstructed from higher resolution representations\n- Transformation: Given a resolution N, construct h from a Gaussian process fit to the base grid points\n- Repair: Meta-repair combining layer clipping and targeted adjustment to maintain both integral and sum constraints\n\n3. Implementation procedure\n- Initialize:\n  * Use parent solution h0 (560 points) with sum=280\n  * Create base hierarchy: [h0, h_quad (1120 pts), h_oct (2240 pts)]\n- Optimization loop:\n  * Phase 1 (coarse): 10-20 iterations with simulated annealing using projected gradients\n  * Phase 2 (medium): 5-10 iterations using Bayesian optimization with Gaussian process surrogate\n  * Phase 3 (fine): 3-5 iterations using local search with adaptive multi-scale gradients\n- Repair details:\n  * Three-stage repair: Clip, adjust to sum constraint, then project to nearest feasible point\n  * For resolution change:\n    - Downsample: Averaging method with nearest neighbor fallback\n    - Upsample: Linear interpolation followed by constrained L2 projection\n  * Objective calculation: Re-evaluate after repair using full correlation spectrum\n\n4. Search choices and useful variations\n- Primary variation: Hierarchical multi-resolution optimization with adaptive resolution cycling\n- Secondary variation: Hierarchical Gaussian Process representation with automatic relevance detection\n- Cooling schedule: Logarithmic temperature decay for simulated annealing (T = T0 * exp(-\u03b1*i))\n- Bayesian optimization kernels: Mat\u00e9rn with automatic relevance detection of the nearest 100 points\n- Minimum resource usage: Time-based early termination checking after every 10th iteration\n\n5. Compute budget and robustness\n- Dominant cost: Gaussian process fitting (O(n\u00b2) for n=2240, dominates total computation)\n- Time estimates:\n  * Score evaluation: Proportional to grid size (560 points: 0.002s, 2240 points: 0.04s)\n  * Repair: O(n log n) for sorting/adjustment (560: 0.0005s, 2240: 0.002s)\n  * Restart metric: Number of invalid candidates repaired after full constraint check\n- Feasibility checks: Ensure all layers satisfy 0 \u2264 h \u2264 1 and sum(h)=280 after each repair\n- Fallback strategy: Return the most recently improved candidate with valid sum constraint\n- Budget strategy: Fix resolution points at 560, 1120, 2240 and cycle between them\n\n6. Validation and return contract\n- Final evaluation:\n  - Confirm valid h with 0 \u2264 h[i] \u2264 1 for all i\n  - Verify sum(h) \u2248 280 (tolerance 1e-12)\n  - Compute h_oct to match resolution\n- Objective score: np.max(np.correlate(h_oct, 1-h_oct, mode='full')*(2.2/n_oct)   [n_oct=2240]\n- Success criteria:\n  - No constraint violations\n  - Score < 0.3808\n  - Representation matches parent resolution otherwise",
